      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "NOT MEASURED (surface display confirmed by design; no functional assay result reported in the cited clip)",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "The paper explicitly names Ala34 as the insertion anchor ('following the signal peptide (Alanine 34)'), and Python lookup confirms seq[33]='A' and seq[34]='S', matching residue_before/after exactly. Position 34 lies 7 residues into the extracellular span (27\u2013168), 135 residues from the TM boundary (169), satisfying all distance constraints. The construct is full-length and membrane-anchored, so the tag is genuinely surface-displayed; insert_after_residue=34 is the direct reading of 'at Alanine 34'. Full-length TMEM123 construct with ALFA tag inserted after Ala34 in the extracellular N-terminal region, following the signal peptide (SP cleavage at residue 26, mature N-terminus at residue 27). The tag was engineered for surface display in a membrane-anchored context, exploiting the predicted unstructured nature of the extracellular domain. [validation: surface_only; position: validated; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "citation": "preprint",
          "claim": "The extracellular region of TMEM123 is predicted to be unstructured, so we added the Alfa tag to the N-terminal region following the signal peptide (Alanine 34) (Fig. 4a)."
        }
      ],
